    {
      "id": "u03-l2",
      "title": "Eleven to thirty & your age",
      "goal": "Say how old you are.",
      "tip": {
        "title": "Avoir … ans",
        "body": "11 to 16 are single words (onze, douze, treize, quatorze, quinze, seize); 17, 18 and 19 are \"ten-seven\" etc.: dix-sept, dix-huit, dix-neuf. 21 is vingt et un, then vingt-deux, vingt-trois… In French you HAVE your age: J'ai vingt ans — never je suis vingt. The t of vingt is silent on its own (\"van\") but spoken in 21–29 (vingt-deux sounds like \"vant-deux\", with a nasal vowel)."
      },
