    {
      "id": "u03-l3",
      "title": "Up to 100 & prices",
      "goal": "Ask what something costs and understand the price.",
      "tip": {
        "title": "Counting in twenties",
        "body": "40 quarante, 50 cinquante, 60 soixante — then France switches to maths: 70 = soixante-dix (60 + 10), 71 = soixante et onze, 80 = quatre-vingts (4 × 20), 81 = quatre-vingt-un (no et, no s), 90 = quatre-vingt-dix (4 × 20 + 10), 100 = cent. Prices: say euros in the middle — 4,50 € = quatre euros cinquante. Watch the liaison: deux_euros, trois_euros, six_euros (\"z\"), vingt_euros (\"t\")."
      },
