    {
      "id": "u03-l4",
      "kind": "grammar",
      "title": "avoir & plurals",
      "goal": "Say what you have — one or many.",
      "tip": {
        "title": "avoir (to have) + plural nouns",
        "body": "avoir: j'ai, tu as, il/elle/on a, nous avons, vous avez, ils/elles ont. Je becomes j' before a vowel (j'ai). Link the s with a \"z\" sound: nous_avons, vous_avez, ils_ont — and don't confuse ils_ont (\"eel-zon\", they have) with ils sont (\"eel-son\", they are). Most plurals just add a silent -s: un chat → deux chats. You usually hear the plural only in the article or number: le chat / les chats. Avoir is also used for age: Il a dix ans."
      },
